proof: redumper-mpf | debian | vendor-cap
date: 2026-07-17
lane/VM: test-debian (Debian 13), repo OBS home:gmipf:media-preservation/Debian_13
user groups: "gmipf sudo audio dip video users netdev scanner bluetooth lpadmin"
             (NO cdrom/disk/plugdev) -> groupless
drive: PLEXTOR DVDR PX-760A (USB 0dc4:0061) -> /dev/sr1, audio CD (20 tracks)
mechanism: Debian setcap in ubuntu/redumper-mpf/debian/redumper-mpf.postinst
           (the postinst-setcap path, delivered by OBS -- the newest cap mechanism)
note: fixed-name pin (was redumper732); the binary moved to /usr/bin/redumper-mpf,
      so the setcap target changed and this line was re-measured, not inherited.

--- delivery (as installed from OBS, never hand-touched) ---
$ /sbin/getcap /usr/bin/redumper-mpf
/usr/bin/redumper-mpf cap_sys_rawio=ep
$ dpkg -S /usr/bin/redumper-mpf -> redumper-mpf: /usr/bin/redumper-mpf   (redumper-mpf 732-1)
$ /usr/bin/redumper-mpf --version -> redumper (build: b732)

--- GREEN (cap present): D8 vendor read reaches the drive ---
$ redumper-mpf disc --verbose --drive=/dev/sr1 --image-path=... --image-name=t
  inquiry: PLEXTOR - DVDR PX-760A (revision level: 1.07, vendor specific: 08/18/07 15:10)
  configuration: PLEXTOR (read offset: +30, C2 shift: 295, pre-gap start: -75,
                 read method: D8, sector order: DATA_C2_SUB)
  lead-in reads (negative LBA, via D8) = 75, "Operation not permitted" = 0,
  lines with "SCSIs: [1-9]" = 0
  last progress: / [  7%] LBA:  20896/277131, errors: { SCSIs: 0, C2s: 0, Q: 35 }
  (run trimmed by `timeout 50`, exit 124)

--- RED (A/B: cap stripped with `setcap -r`, then restored) ---
$ sudo setcap -r /usr/bin/redumper-mpf ; getcap -> ''      # cap gone
$ redumper-mpf disc ... (same command)
- [  0%] LBA:    -75/277131, errors: { SCSIs: 0, C2s: 0, Q: 0 }error: SYSTEM (Operation not permitted)
  exit 255 ; "Operation not permitted" hits = 1     # EPERM at the first D8 read
$ sudo setcap cap_sys_rawio=ep /usr/bin/redumper-mpf ; getcap -> cap_sys_rawio=ep   # restored

VERDICT: PROVEN. The postinst-delivered cap on the renamed binary is load-bearing:
with it the D8 lead-in read (-75..-1) succeeds groupless; without it the identical
read fails EPERM at LBA -75.
